<title>USA: Gilead's Vistide approved in Europe.</title>
<headline>Gilead's Vistide approved in Europe.</headline>
<dateline>FOSTER CITY, Calif. 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gilead Sciences Inc said Thursday that the European Commission cleared its Vistide drug for late-stage AIDS patients for marketing in the 15 countries that make up the European Union.</p>
<p>Vistide is a treatment for CMV retinitis, a rapidly progressing viral infection that strikes AIDS patients and can lead to blindness. The drug was approved in the U.S. last June.</p>
<p>Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn Inc has exclusive marketing rights for Vistide outside of the United States.</p>
